      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Short answer: No.\nLong answer:\nThe most important thing in social platforms is that newcomers can quickly find the active part of the community.\nOne of the major problems VRChat is currently facing is that most \"regulars\" are hidden away from newcomers off in private instances. Meaning in order for a new user to \"become\" a regular, they must first meet and befriend a regular who just happened to have been in public, which is rare. This is a big problem. A common cite to people trying out VRChat is they just can't find their crowd. Rather than tough it out and try to make friends, they are far more likely to not return after trying VRChat only once.\nThe feature suggested here not only does not fix this major problem with VRChat, it would magnify the problem even more.\nSo no, absolutely not - this would be very bad for VRChat.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
