  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-24T00:28:53.540Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "(TL;DR on last paragraph)\n\nI traverse public lobbies all the time. Some worlds are better than others with user behavior, but it seems like a majority of users who are being a disturbance or being uncivil, are the ones who are either Visitor rank or have not registered a VRChat account yet (Steam/Meta/four digits). Even though it is possible to utilize custom Safety Settings to mute or hide avatars for everyone in that rank, I do not think it is fair to anybody who wants to genuinely enter the community. I am aware that trolls and hackers can be committed to ranking up their account, and that anyone at any rank can be nasty, but having an instance filter will simply narrow down the problem with people in lobbies being disrespectful, and more people can pay attention to what's happening around them.\nMany of these lobbies contain children under the age of 13 (violation of Section 2 of VRCToS), and primarily all of them are not on a registered account. Currently, there is an ongoing “Photon bot” crasher problem where those accounts are not verified. See also my thread on Unverified accounts: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/add-unverified-tag-on-steamoculus-account-nameplate-hud-hide-four-digits\nTL;DR To keep public lobbies a more enjoyable experience for regulars, I would like to suggest the presentation of \"Public+\" lobbies. I propose that these lobbies can be accessed only by users with a registered VRChat account, and are ranked as New User and above.",
